#!/bin/bash
# land-gemstones-tab.sh — the Astrology Zone gets a gem marketplace, and the
# stones move out of the remedies page onto it.
#
# Thirty stones with the owner's own photographs; a chart names at most five.
# Every one carries the finger, the hand, the metal and the day it is worn.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# INCLUDES 30 BINARY IMAGES — the patch is large; that is expected.
# PRECONDITION: land-budget-is-a-target.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="One surface prescribes a stone"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A budget is a target, not only a ceiling"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-budget-is-a-target.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="930394fbfb94002ef15995bbf45c412c8a6617fab58cf422ac162fda12538a44"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied — 30 stone photographs and both sides of the marketplace"

echo "== the catalogue regenerates from the owner's card file, byte for byte"
cd together-city-chat
node scripts/gen-gem-catalog.mjs
git diff --quiet -- src/astrology/gems/gem-catalog.ts || {
  echo "!! gem-catalog.ts does not match its generator. Nothing committed."; exit 1; }

echo "== gates: the API"
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/src/astrology/gems \
        together-city-chat/scripts/gen-gem-catalog.mjs \
        together-city-chat/src/astrology/gem-remedy-content.ts \
        together-city-chat/src/astrology/astrology.service.ts \
        together-city-chat/src/astrology/astrology.controller.ts \
        together-city-react/public/assets/gems \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/app/router.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/config/hubs.ts \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
One surface prescribes a stone

The Astrology Zone already recommended gemstones. It did it on a page called
Gems & Remedies that has no entry in the sidebar — a live prescription, reading
the running dasha lord and nothing else, that no citizen could reach from the
menu. Adding a Gemstones tab beside it would have made two engines answering
"which stone is mine" from two different readings, both confident, disagreeing
in public. So the marketplace takes the stones and the remedies page keeps the
practices, which were always its own.

The new engine reads what the chart engine has been computing all along:

  LIFE      the lagna lord's stone, from the ascendant
  FORTUNE   the ninth lord's stone
  PERIOD    the running mahadasha lord's — the season, not the birth
  MOON      the moon rashi's lord, and the fallback when there is no birth time
  NUMBER    the life-path number's stone, from a different tradition, said so

A stone holds ONE role, the highest it qualifies for, with every reason it
earned printed under it. Leo lagna in a Sun mahadasha with life path 1 is three
separate routes to ruby, and the first version of this listed ruby three times
and looked exactly like a shop padding a page. Thirty stones exist; a chart
names at most five, and the other twenty-five are not shown because they are not
yours. A marketplace that opens on the whole shelf is a jewellery site with an
astrology theme.

Every card says which FINGER, which hand, which metal and which day — the first
question anybody asks about a prescribed stone, and until now the answer lived
only on the page with no way in.

That table was the same failure one layer down. Nine rows existed twice: once in
gem-remedy-content.ts and once inside the owner's ring-studio file. They agreed
on eight planets and disagreed about Ketu — little finger in one, middle finger
in the other, Thursday in one and "Tuesday or Thursday" in the other. Nothing
was broken, because two pages nobody compares side by side had one row each.
There is one table now, wearing.ts, the ring studio's values as the later and
richer set, and a test asserting the old file derives from it row for row.

Also here:

  · The thirty photographs, lifted out of the owner's stone-pages HTML where
    they were embedded as data URIs, keyed by stone id. They carry `no-case` —
    relief.css frames every photograph and provides that exemption for pictures
    already composed, which cut-out stones on white plainly are.
  · The substitutes. A diamond is 150,000 a carat and a white sapphire is 6,000;
    a page that answers "which stone" honestly and "what it costs" not at all is
    half an answer.
  · The 72-hour trial note, on blue sapphire, hessonite and cat's eye, travelling
    with the recommendation so no surface can forget to print it.
  · No birth time removes the two stones that need an ascendant and says so. It
    does not compute them from a noon chart and present the result as fact.

The catalogue is GENERATED from the owner's card database by
scripts/gen-gem-catalog.mjs, and the gate re-runs the generator and fails if the
committed file has drifted from it. What is not here is a carat weight: the next
screen is a weight and a quality slider, the recommended weight is the one field
the owner's data has not reached us yet, and a page that picks a number on
somebody's behalf for a 90,000 stone is worse than no page. So there is no
"design this stone" button, and its absence is the point.
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: One surface prescribes a stone
 Both sides — push, then give Railway a minute before opening
 Astrology → Gemstones.
===============================================================

DONE
